    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d702">

                <pb facs="0773" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.24/10–344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                            State to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-03">October 3,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I attach a copy of the memorandum which I sent on September 11<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d702-f1"/> and which was given to you at Quebec by Mr.
                        Hopkins.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d702-f2"/> This memorandum <pb facs="0774"
                        n="762" xml:id="pg762"/> suggested a basis for a Lend-Lease agreement with
                    France differing somewhat from that set forth in my memorandum of July 15, 1944,
                    which you approved on July 18. I also attach a copy of this memorandum.<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d702-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I understand that you requested Mr. Morgenthau<anchor n="14" xml:id="d702-f4"/>
                    to discuss this matter with me and with Mr. Hopkins. Before Mr. Morgenthau had
                    an opportunity to discuss this question with us you approved on September 15 a
                        memorandum<anchor n="15" xml:id="d702-f5"/> which recommended indefinite
                    postponement.</p>
                <p>I wish to recall that on the basis of your July 18 approval we reached agreement
                    with the French on August 25 to continue negotiations on Lend-Lease with a view
                    to reaching agreement prior to its conclusion.</p>
                <p>My staff is under almost daily pressure from the French to submit a draft
                    agreement for discussion. Whatever may be your decision on the memorandum of
                    September 11, we are under obligations to proceed in some way.</p>
                <p>I would point out to you that in the draft upon which my memorandum of September
                    11 was based, there are four articles, VI, VII, VIII, IX, in which the Treasury
                    has a specific responsibility. These they approved.</p>
                <p>I hope very much, therefore, that you will authorize me to proceed to negotiate
                    with the French on the basis which you decide is appropriate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
